From 91ba2d9a01c0ee49cca54a7832e0066ea162764a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:25:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Go on without the EZ2STR and map-sky managers when they
 cannot be allocated

app_init_managers loaded both managers through their instance
functions, which allocate on first use and return NULL when
mem_try_alloc fails, and passed that NULL to the load:
map_sky_mgr_load reads self->lua, and ez2_str_effect_mgr_load writes
self->rows once its file has loaded. The loads are skipped now, so
startup goes on without the two managers, as when their files do not
load; the load results were not looked at before either.

Their later users ask the instance again, which retries the allocation
and gives NULL while memory is short. They now take a missing manager
as one whose file did not load:
- map_sky_mgr_apply (game mode initialisation, every map) finds no sky
  data and sets the black background;
- ez2_str_effect_mgr_get_effect_ids (effect registration),
  ez2_str_effect_mgr_find_by_effect_id (Ez2StrEffectEx init) and
  ez2_str_effect_mgr_get_effect_id (skill actions, Hyper Novice) find
  no rows (an empty list, NULL, -1), which their callers already handle.

The new test_manager_alloc_failure runs the startup loads, the two
instances, the map-sky load and apply and the EZ2STR lookups extracted
from production with an allocator that fails: no load may be called with
NULL, and the users must answer as for unloaded managers; then, with
memory, both loads must run. It fails on the previous code with any one
of the three files reverted (the EZ2STR load called with NULL, or an
access violation in map_sky_mgr_apply or the lookups).

Also found, not fixed: app_init_managers loads four more managers the
same way (repute_mgr_load, item_db_to_id_load, item_reform_mgr_load,
enchant_mgr_load), each dereferencing a NULL instance; their 33 later
users would need the same check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
